ntScenarioAxis_xelb_LiquidAssetCovenantRequirementAfterFirstOutObligationsAreFullyPaidMember_Mbunw_ZmEUqQzeQ_4qV7fg" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xelb:DebtCovenantLiquidityRequirement" scale="6" id="Narr_4PwBbIKghUaTqlHree-GNw"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="As_Of_3_20_2026_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_xelb_LiquidAssetCovenantRequirementAfterFirstOutObligationsAreFullyPaidMember_SEGCZwDqykWKF69ZWV1SXg" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xelb:DebtCovenantLiquidityRequirement" scale="6" id="Narr_BDZZgvZSK0yTlHO637_0CQ">0</ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction>; and (iv) the transaction closing date was extended to March 24, 2026.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">On April 13, 2026, the Company entered into the seventh amendment to the loan and security agreement with the term loan debt lenders and FEAC, which provided for, among other things: the ability of the Company to consummate the issuance of certain senior secured notes (as described below); the ability for IPX to convert its $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="As_Of_4_13_2026_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_xelb_TermLoanaMember_7QwEEWxYBUaPMZCv6Rz7ZQ" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentCarryingAmount" scale="6" id="Narr_xrlfkrWVyUuF39hP8w_Bjw">0.5</ix:nonFraction>0 million Term Loan A to common shares of the Company at the price per share equal to $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Divide_USD_shares_IzeRNIPzn0yyfOr7CryysQ" contextRef="As_Of_4_13_2026_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_xelb_TermLoanaMember_7QwEEWxYBUaPMZCv6Rz7ZQ" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:SharePrice" scale="0" id="Narr_yBzX3Yrozk-1oUqziCJnwQ">1.35</ix:nonFraction>, subject to adjustment; modifications to certain payment terms; modifications to certain financial covenants; modifications to certain financial reporting requirements; and the amendment of the FEAC&#8217;s role to include certain limitations. In connection with the seventh amendment, FEAC&#8217;s affiliated lenders entered into agreements whereby a $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="As_Of_4_13_2026_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_xelb_TermLoanaMember_7QwEEWxYBUaPMZCv6Rz7ZQ" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentCarryingAmount" scale="6" id="Narr_wt7q12LLmECz4ICMK36f0g">0.5</ix:nonFraction>0 million portion of Term Loan A was sold and assigned to IPX, and the entirety of Term Loan B was sold and assigned to UTG. Additionally, the Company was relieved of its obligation to pay the remaining $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="As_Of_4_13_2026_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_xelb_TermLoanaMember_7QwEEWxYBUaPMZCv6Rz7ZQ" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentFeeAmount" scale="6" id="Narr_Z3rDnvl2bE6PeULIaStlfg">0.325</ix:nonFraction> million amendment fee as specified in the fourth amendment. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;">With respect to the April 13, 2026 changes in terms related to the $0.50 million of Term Loan A debt held by IPX, and considering that IPX was a common lender for both a portion of the Term Loan A debt and a portion of the new senior secured notes (as described below), the Company evaluated and determined that the changes related to the debt held by </p></ix:continuation></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">14</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:79.3%;border:0;margin:30pt 10.35% 30pt 10.35%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:10.35%;padding-right:10.35%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;min-height:41.75pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 30pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;">XCEL BRANDS,&#160;INC. AND SUBSIDIARIES</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;">Notes&#160;to Unaudited Condensed Consolidated Financial Statements</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;">June 30, 2026</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">(Unaudited)</p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><ix:continuation id="Tb_D3S1xLeRkEyBBqFBWcEUeg_cont2" continuedAt="Tb_D3S1xLeRkEyBBqFBWcEUeg_cont3"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">IPX represented an extinguishment under ASC 470-50. Accordingly, the Company recognized a $0.01 million loss on early extinguishment of debt for the three and six months ended June 30, 2026, due to the write-off of unamortized deferred finance costs related to such debt. The Company also evaluated the aforementioned conversion feature that was added to the Term Loan A debt held by IPX, and determined that it is not required to be separated and accounted for as a derivative under ASC 815; the Term Loan A debt is being accounted for as a single liability under ASC 470-20.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Also on April 13, 2026, the Company repaid a total of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="Duration_4_13_2026_To_4_13_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_FirstEagleAlternativeCreditLlcMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_xelb_TermLoanaMember_LxzYaRtDzkOwdtwIpYKqwg" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:RepaymentsOfLongTermDebt" scale="6" id="Narr_-EDvp3LLyEutFACKEdARpA">3.25</ix:nonFraction> million of Term Loan A debt &#8211; of which, $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="Duration_4_13_2026_To_4_13_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_FirstEagleAlternativeCreditLlcMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_xelb_TermLoanaMember_LxzYaRtDzkOwdtwIpYKqwg" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xelb:RepaymentsOfLongTermDebtUsingProceedsFromAnotherDebt" scale="6" id="Narr_N73g4DlfWkuNp4C70IE9UA">2.25</ix:nonFraction> million was repaid using the net proceeds received from the issuance of the senior secured notes (as described below) and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="Duration_4_13_2026_To_4_13_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_FirstEagleAlternativeCreditLlcMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_xelb_TermLoanaMember_LxzYaRtDzkOwdtwIpYKqwg" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xelb:RepaymentsOfLongTermDebtUsingRestrictedCash" scale="6" id="Narr_dTnyxus3c0CHuw0EzBVVpQ">1.00</ix:nonFraction> million was paid with the Company&#8217;s restricted cash. This resulted in the repayment of all remaining principal owed to FEAC under the term loans; in connection with this repayment, the Company paid $0.14 million of fees to FEAC, which were recorded as loss on early extinguishment of debt for the three and six months ended June 30, 2026. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;">Principal</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">As of June 30, 2026, the remaining principal balance of Term Loan A was $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_xelb_TermLoanaMember_e5iZnFn4bkez4itG1A_Mcg" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentCarryingAmount" scale="6" id="Narr_tF2DMKzAdE-eGh2OcgIdbg">0.50</ix:nonFraction> million and is due on September 20, 2027. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">As of June 30, 2026, the remaining principal balance of Term Loan B was $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_xelb_TermLoanbMember_fWEaxw_4xEy4-zMw5eyYkA" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentCarryingAmount" scale="6" id="Narr_b2iupOsWPkCEYi6tmZsTvw">10.35</ix:nonFraction> million (which includes $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_xelb_TermLoanbMember_fWEaxw_4xEy4-zMw5eyYkA" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xelb:LongTermDebtPrincipalDue" scale="6" id="Narr_EAyDd6W6wESULt5hgxU9OA">9.12</ix:nonFraction> million of original proceeds borrowed plus $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_xelb_TermLoanbMember_fWEaxw_4xEy4-zMw5eyYkA" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xelb:LongTermDebtAccumulatedPaidInKindInterest" scale="6" id="Narr_lxAzHJg5tUeQteKHTzz9OA">1.23</ix:nonFraction> million of accumulated paid in-kind (&#8220;PIK&#8221;) interest, as discussed below) and is due at the maturity date of December 12, 2028.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;">Interest</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">From December 12, 2024 through April 20, 2025, interest on Term Loans accrued at an annual rate equal to the secured overnight financing rate as administered by the Federal Reserve Bank of New York for an interest period equal to three months (the &#8220;3-month SOFR rate&#8221;), subject to a <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_gw05YkuTH0WwOqVaqC56mg" contextRef="As_Of_12_12_2024_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_FirstEagleAlternativeCreditLlcMember_DbK6m0ZcXkmpNVtWjgVS-Q" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentInterestRateStatedPercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_jHlp_ArDc0ChL9lAbBBGwQ">2.0</ix:nonFraction>% floor, plus (i) <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_gw05YkuTH0WwOqVaqC56mg" contextRef="As_Of_12_12_2024_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_FirstEagleAlternativeCreditLlcMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_xelb_TermLoanaMember_ke3molTUPka33-C_HDYNFA" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DerivativeBasisSpreadOnVariableRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_FQ1bL6XRzkO1c3A0MjP_5w">8.5</ix:nonFraction>% for Term Loan A and <span style="-sec-ix-hidden:Hidden_MbVHQwCcQU6kSS5i-WyLUg;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Delayed</span></span> Draw Term Loan and (ii) <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_gw05YkuTH0WwOqVaqC56mg" contextRef="As_Of_12_12_2024_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_FirstEagleAlternativeCreditLlcMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_xelb_TermLoanbMember__Y2ORSjRME6ANkQlygGRTQ" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DerivativeBasisSpreadOnVariableRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_ESBTbVeQt0Stwxqkp3t2Ng">13.5</ix:nonFraction>% for Term Loan B. From and after April 21, 2025, interest on the Term Loans accrues at an annual rate equal to the 3-month SOFR rate, subject to a <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_gw05YkuTH0WwOqVaqC56mg" contextRef="As_Of_4_21_2025_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_FirstEagleAlternativeCreditLlcMember_Jd9PULNyQkihwMdwyvP_4Q" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentInterestRateStatedPercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_HDBPFC5WI0ujWarZ5kT2gQ">2.0</ix:nonFraction>% floor, plus (i) <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_gw05YkuTH0WwOqVaqC56mg" contextRef="As_Of_4_21_2025_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_FirstEagleAlternativeCreditLlcMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_xelb_TermLoanaMember_hRLpEJw2RkywnkqdUzy6cA" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DerivativeBasisSpreadOnVariableRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_mbqqxiejbEOY9qZ45xIMpg">8.5</ix:nonFraction>% for Term Loan A and (ii) <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_gw05YkuTH0WwOqVaqC56mg" contextRef="As_Of_4_21_2025_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_FirstEagleAlternativeCreditLlcMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_xelb_TermLoanbMember_5IrRXUDoKUyXmfFWrglfBw" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DerivativeBasisSpreadOnVariableRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_HBPHv2_aaU2uEQ8yKmYaHg">6.5</ix:nonFraction>% for Term Loan B. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Interest on amounts outstanding under the Term Loans accrues daily and is payable at the end of each calendar month, except that from April 21, 2025 through March 31, 2027, interest on the Term Loan B will be paid in-kind (&#8220;PIK&#8221;) by being capitalized and added to the principal amount of the Term Loan B at the end of each calendar month. For the current quarter and current six months, the Company recognized PIK interest approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_IJJ3Na3OCU64V3a7kPgdOg" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:PaidInKindInterest" scale="6" id="Narr_cttVbpazpk641p3avBuF3Q">0.26</ix:nonFraction> million and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_AOf8Oz5EykGUyJMcCLhuDw" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:PaidInKindInterest" scale="6" id="Narr_47EG4jX3kECPvnDlLS2oXw">0.52</ix:nonFraction> million, respectively. For the prior year quarter and prior year six months, the Company recognized approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_6_30_2025_COhOUwyIe0aQWScTfXbySA" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:PaidInKindInterest" scale="6" id="Narr_3a5DL6FfD0Ks5wTd7Kt6tQ"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2025_To_6_30_2025_C9qxWStCm0SeKC3hX1BVNA" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:PaidInKindInterest" scale="6" id="Narr_7xHIaV9St06a2mc9_uT3gg">0.19</ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction> million of PIK interest. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">For the current quarter and current six months, the Company incurred interest expense (including interest paid in cash, PIK, and the amortization of deferred finance costs) related to term loan debt of approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_xelb_NewTermLoanDebtMember_5PkFa44ZQkuRf2OTO9qPQQ" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:InterestExpenseNonoperating" scale="6" id="Narr_TJuI86p64EWyfeSTS2gWSQ">0.42</ix:nonFraction> million and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_xelb_NewTermLoanDebtMember_ECUYo6tpP0Oe29zVR_EbnA" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:InterestExpenseNonoperating" scale="6" id="Narr_TeCuTrrRw0yT3mxWkTjGqw">0.91</ix:nonFraction> million, respectively. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="background:#ffffff;">For the prior year quarter and prior year six months, the Company incurred total interest expense (including interest paid in cash, PIK, and the amortization of deferred finance costs) related to term loan debt of approximately </span><span style="background:#ffffff;">$</span><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2025_To_6_30_2025_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_xelb_NewTermLoanDebtMember_aEdMTheljkme7wRTbOMsEw" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:InterestExpenseNonoperating" scale="6" id="Narr_KPiQPWqseE6_YvP00XIy2w">0.46</ix:nonFraction><span style="background:#ffffff;">&#160;million and </span><span style="background:#ffffff;">$</span><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_6_30_2025_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_xelb_NewTermLoanDebtMember_-urJUP1ox0-c9ZM1mMC8dA" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:InterestExpenseNonoperating" scale="6" id="Narr_sGY0JxarrESsgpEWmxlIYw">0.93</ix:nonFraction><span style="background:#ffffff;">&#160;million, respectively.</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;">Exit Fees</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;">The amended loan agreement also requires that the Company pay an exit fee of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_FirstEagleAlternativeCreditLlcMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_xelb_TermLoanaMember_5OVE8YYSWE6JgrqE_oQb_w" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentFeeAmount" scale="6" id="Narr_IBCnqrfo90ySJ_TIoIHFzQ">0.175</ix:nonFraction> million to FEAC related to Term Loan A and an exit fee of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_RestoreCapitalLlcMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_xelb_TermLoanbMember_QuGLSg0NeU69NrBxk6ydPw" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentFeeAmount" scale="6" id="Narr_Dgk-EgwOVkm9aWB2HmWuhg">0.40</ix:nonFraction> million to Restore related to Term Loan B upon the maturity or full payment of the Term Loans. The Company recognized the cost of the Term Loan A exit fee over the remaining term of the related debt, while </p></ix:continuation></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">15</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:79.3%;border:0;margin:30pt 10.35% 30pt 10.35%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:10.35%;padding-right:10.35%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;min-height:41.75pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 30pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;">XCEL BRANDS,&#160;INC. AND SUBSIDIARIES</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;">Notes&#160;to Unaudited Condensed Consolidated Financial Statements</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;">June 30, 2026</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">(Unaudited)</p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><ix:continuation id="Tb_D3S1xLeRkEyBBqFBWcEUeg_cont3" continuedAt="Tb_D3S1xLeRkEyBBqFBWcEUeg_cont4"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">the net present value of the Term Loan B exit fee on April 21, 2025 was recognized as part of the loss on early extinguishment of debt recorded in the second quarter of 2025. As of June 30, 2026, the amount of accrued exit fees with respect to Term Loan A was $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_xelb_TermLoanaMember_e5iZnFn4bkez4itG1A_Mcg" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xelb:AccruedExitFeesCurrent" scale="6" id="Narr_q8RbZS3t_k-1PmKQBi1zTA">0.13</ix:nonFraction> million, while the amount of accrued exit fees with respect to Term Loan B was $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_xelb_TermLoanbMember_fWEaxw_4xEy4-zMw5eyYkA" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xelb:AccruedExitFeesNoncurrent" scale="6" id="Narr_gw8t6AGG80qdZnWnib_ebA">0.32</ix:nonFraction> million; both amounts are presented within Other long-term liabilities on the condensed consolidated balance sheet as of June 30, 2026. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;">Deferred Finance Costs and Other Reductions to Carrying Value of Debt</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">In connection with entering into the Term Loans in December 2024, the Company incurred loan origination fees, plus various legal and other fees; these fees and costs totaling $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="As_Of_12_12_2024_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_FirstEagleAlternativeCreditLlcMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_xelb_NewTermLoanDebtMember_oC9a7rlzk0yzeZXkzlHnjw" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DeferredFinanceCostsGross" scale="6" id="Narr_McCnXvW850Krfr970hlBJA">0.92</ix:nonFraction> million were deferred on the Company&#8217;s balance sheet as a reduction of the carrying value of the term loan debt. Also in connection with entering into the Term Loans in December 2024, the Company issued certain warrants to the lenders to purchase shares of the Company&#8217;s common stock. In accordance with applicable GAAP, the Company allocated the value of the total proceeds of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="As_Of_12_12_2024_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xelb_NewLoanAndSecurityAgreementMember_rP-DEL8NlU29s3PRYIprnw" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentCarryingAmount" scale="6" id="Narr_fcHaQ3an1UGUzuTi2tqCuQ">10.0</ix:nonFraction> million between the term loan debt and the warrants, based on the relative fair values of each; as a result, the Company recognized a $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="Duration_12_12_2024_To_12_12_2024_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_FirstEagleAlternativeCreditLlcMember_glMXUiKpiEqKAIbifrdzFg" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ProceedsFromIssuanceOfWarrants" scale="6" id="Narr_zKZQMjnkWEOMBCaLGC-VDA">0.48</ix:nonFraction> million increase to stockholders&#8217; equity as additional paid-in capital for the allocated fair value of the warrants, and an offsetting decrease to the net carrying value of the term loan debt. From December 12, 2024, and through April 20, 2025, these reductions to the carrying value of the term loan debt totaling $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_FirstEagleAlternativeCreditLlcMember_fLMVZhkPP0iZNk6wKCS0TA" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:AmortizationOfDebtDiscountPremium" scale="6" id="Narr_i1kbutgSvUiwUjdVSoy5XA">1.40</ix:nonFraction> million were being amortized to interest expense over the term of the debt using the effective interest method. The $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="Duration_4_21_2025_To_4_21_2025_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_xelb_NewTermLoanDebtMember_YrPDFPcvn0uii_mX6rAlwA" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:WriteOffOfDeferredDebtIssuanceCost" scale="6" id="Narr_ziEXYcSzCUmHF_1ofoMJaw">1.26</ix:nonFraction> million remaining unamortized balance of such amounts was written-off as part of the loss on early extinguishment of debt upon the closing of the April 21, 2025 debt refinancing. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;">In connection with the debt refinancing transaction on April 21, 2025, the Company incurred certain legal costs and other fees; these fees and costs totaling $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="As_Of_4_21_2025_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_FirstEagleAlternativeCreditLlcMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_xelb_NewTermLoanDebtMember_Hhnn4EcpjUSemAR3rzhZFg" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DeferredFinanceCostsGross" scale="6" id="Narr_cSHjHhlsk0axdOY4PIxQdg">0.53</ix:nonFraction> million were deferred on the Company&#8217;s balance sheet as a reduction of the carrying value of the term loan debt. Also in connection with the April 21, 2025 debt refinancing transaction, the Company issued certain warrants to UTG to purchase shares of the Company&#8217;s common stock. In accordance with GAAP, the Company allocated the value of the total proceeds of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="As_Of_4_21_2025_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xelb_NewLoanAndSecurityAgreementMember_K4abfFZdoUKFQDOJiu_tIA" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentCarryingAmount" scale="6" id="Narr_5oNinmXS0kewO8oBPKjW3g">13.62</ix:nonFraction> million between the term loan debt and the warrants, based on the relative fair values of each; as a result, the Company recognized a $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="Duration_4_21_2025_To_4_21_2025_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_FirstEagleAlternativeCreditLlcMember_JpptNU1h6kO-NUrQNewZfg" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ProceedsFromIssuanceOfWarrants" scale="6" id="Narr_93yRuRQcukW9cPqRSm7Yzw">0.58</ix:nonFraction> million increase to stockholders&#8217; equity as additional paid-in capital for the allocated fair value of the warrants, and an offsetting decrease to the net carrying value of the term loan debt. These reductions to the carrying value of the term loan debt totaling $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="Duration_4_21_2025_To_4_21_2025_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_FirstEagleAlternativeCreditLlcMember_JpptNU1h6kO-NUrQNewZfg" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:AmortizationOfDebtDiscountPremium" scale="6" id="Narr_HtTgITZvU0eU7OPcax7ojg">1.11</ix:nonFraction> million are being amortized to interest expense over the term of the debt using the effective interest method.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="margin-bottom:12pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;text-decoration-color:#000000;text-decoration-line:underline;text-decoration-style:solid;">Senior Secured Notes</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="margin-bottom:12pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;">On April 13, 2026, the Company entered into certain agreements with Smithline Family Trust II (&#8220;SFT&#8221;), Quick Capital, LLC (&#8220;Quick&#8221;), and IPX (collectively, the &#8220;Purchasers&#8221;), pursuant to which the Company issued and sold to the Purchasers <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_gw05YkuTH0WwOqVaqC56mg" contextRef="As_Of_4_13_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_PurchasersMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_SeniorNotesMember_b4THQhtGskesRAlYwKPXQQ" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentInterestRateStatedPercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_p2yClOcHGUmgkixra0kdUg">12.5</ix:nonFraction>% Senior Secured Notes due April 13, 2027 in the original principal amount of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="As_Of_4_13_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_PurchasersMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_SeniorNotesMember_b4THQhtGskesRAlYwKPXQQ" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:SeniorNotes" scale="0" id="Narr_JGCGFTyTYECf2fZt-D7d_A">3,005,780</ix:nonFraction> (the &#8220;Secured Notes&#8221;) and <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_aOdaQld8FkuFmrvdGtgC-w" contextRef="Duration_4_13_2026_To_4_13_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_PurchasersMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_SeniorNotesMember_VOsT1WRvVkiRGxS41005Jg" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xelb:StockIssuedDuringPeriodSharesIssuanceWithDebt" scale="0" id="Narr_U9NNvbup70SK5r7EhLjW4A">100,579</ix:nonFraction> shares of the Company&#8217;s common stock. The Secured Notes were issued with an original issue discount, such that the net cash proceeds received by the Company after the discount were $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="Duration_4_13_2026_To_4_13_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_PurchasersMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_SeniorNotesMember_VOsT1WRvVkiRGxS41005Jg" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ProceedsFromSecuredNotesPayable" scale="6" id="Narr_59RMWljidEOMVmIuYVynBg">2.60</ix:nonFraction> million. The Company&#8217;s obligations under the Secured Notes are guaranteed by certain direct and indirect subsidiaries of the Company pursuant to a subsidiary guarantee, and are secured by the assets of the Company and the subsidiary guarantors pursuant to a security agreement.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="margin-bottom:12pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;">At any time after the occurrence of an event of default under the Secured Notes and for so long as such event of default is continuing, the Secured Notes are convertible into shares of common stock of the Company (i) initially at a fixed conversion price equal to $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Divide_USD_shares_IzeRNIPzn0yyfOr7CryysQ" contextRef="As_Of_4_13_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_PurchasersMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_SeniorNotesMember_b4THQhtGskesRAlYwKPXQQ" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentConvertibleConversionPrice1" scale="0" id="Narr_H1bxWjB0IkGluuGLgoY4ZQ">1.165</ix:nonFraction> per share in the case of SFT and Quick or $1.435 per share in the case of IPX, and (ii) after May 17, 2026, at a price equal to the lesser of (a) <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_gw05YkuTH0WwOqVaqC56mg" contextRef="Duration_5_17_2026_To_5_17_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_PurchasersMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_SeniorNotesMember_mvPn8nuFzEipU8_U5v7PpQ" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentConvertibleConversionRatio1" scale="0" id="Narr_hXZEXk-amE6RNcHRtmeSqA">85</ix:nonFraction>% multiplied by the lowest volume weighted average price of the common stock during the 10-trading day period prior to conversion and (b) $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Divide_USD_shares_IzeRNIPzn0yyfOr7CryysQ" contextRef="As_Of_5_17_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_PurchasersMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_SeniorNotesMember_Fjr1lp0cYEek1tycDEHN7g" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentConvertibleConversionPrice1" scale="0" id="Narr_U42HuG-8gUWkxa3Pt_Qw5A">1.165</ix:nonFraction> in the case of SFT and Quick or $1.435 per share in the case of IPX. In addition, to the extent that Company is listed on the Nasdaq Capital Market, the aggregate number of shares of common stock issuable to the Purchasers and any subsequent holder of the Secured Note shall not exceed <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_gw05YkuTH0WwOqVaqC56mg" contextRef="Duration_4_13_2026_To_4_13_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_PurchasersMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_SeniorNotesMember_VOsT1WRvVkiRGxS41005Jg" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xelb:MaximumSharesHoldablePercentage" scale="0" id="Narr_0Ub_kDgLvUyFUHWmVGOLdg">19.99</ix:nonFraction>% of the total number of shares of common stock outstanding or of the voting power of the common </p></ix:continuation></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">16</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:79.3%;border:0;margin:30pt 10.35% 30pt 10.35%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:10.35%;padding-right:10.35%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;min-height:41.75pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 30pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;">XCEL BRANDS,&#160;INC. AND SUBSIDIARIES</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;">Notes&#160;to Unaudited Condensed Consolidated Financial Statements</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;">June 30, 2026</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">(Unaudited)</p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><ix:continuation id="Tb_D3S1xLeRkEyBBqFBWcEUeg_cont4"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">stock as of April 13, 2026 less the shares issued pursuant to the securities purchase agreement unless the Company has obtained stockholder approval in compliance with Nasdaq Listing Rule 5635(d) to authorize the issuance of shares of common stock in connection with the conversion or exchange of all Secured Notes.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="margin-bottom:12pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;">Under the conversion feature described above, because the post-May 17, 2026 conversion price varies with the market price of the Company&#8217;s common stock, this feature is not considered indexed to the Company&#8217;s own stock under ASC 815-40 and therefore represents an embedded derivative. As the feature is exercisable only upon an event of default, and management considers the likelihood of such an occurrence to be remote, the Company concluded that the fair value of the embedded derivative was not material and has therefore not recorded a separate liability. The Company will reassess this conclusion each reporting period. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="margin-bottom:12pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Fees incurred in connection with the transactions described above were approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="As_Of_4_13_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_PurchasersMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_SeniorNotesMember_b4THQhtGskesRAlYwKPXQQ" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentFeeAmount" scale="6" id="Narr_ByzarYZfDkihIngFYcs1Vg">0.1</ix:nonFraction> million.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">As part of the transactions described above, IPX (a related party) purchased $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="As_Of_4_13_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_IpxCapitalLlcMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_SeniorNotesMember_7nwrArEb0UK0p7_JChcDbA" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:SeniorNotes" scale="0" id="Narr_gF-odSV4lkKhKMnGw3sAsw">57,803</ix:nonFraction> original principal amount of the Secured Notes and purchased <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_aOdaQld8FkuFmrvdGtgC-w" contextRef="As_Of_4_13_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_IpxCapitalLlcMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_SeniorNotesMember_7nwrArEb0UK0p7_JChcDbA" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:CommonStockSharesIssued" scale="0" id="Narr_ryItPO82xkCnBt0iE_-TVg">1,742</ix:nonFraction> shares of common stock, on the same terms as the other Purchasers, except that the shares of common stock purchased by IPX were priced at current market value. &#160;</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;">Principal</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Company is required to make $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="Duration_10_13_2026_To_10_13_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_PurchasersMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_SeniorNotesMember_65ju5GIwYUmHkKpieuW1uw" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentPeriodicPayment" scale="6" id="Narr_NmS-tJfg00KIEgQdpejDbw">0.10</ix:nonFraction> million monthly payments on the Secured Notes commencing October 13, 2026, with the balance due at maturity. In addition, the terms of the Secured Notes require mandatory prepayments in certain specified situations, including the sale of any brand or license, or the sale of any debt or equity securities by the Company.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Company made additional principal payments to the lenders during the current quarter and current six months totaling $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_PurchasersMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_SeniorNotesMember_RwpB_mY_qk-VYz6u79Pl8Q" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:RepaymentsOfLongTermDebt" scale="6" id="Narr_jymEuFFgY0uw1xmK_bbtHQ"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_PurchasersMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_SeniorNotesMember_b3MD9YawRkimwBbHRaIr7w" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:RepaymentsOfLongTermDebt" scale="6" id="Narr_lyZtvcFlKk2UtHcdSTp0SA">0.45</ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction> million. The remaining principal balance due under the Secured Notes at June 30, 2026 was $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_PurchasersMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_SeniorNotesMember_5IVP0rdyNk2iM2ER-I-CNQ" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentCarryingAmount" scale="6" id="Narr_muFebKd89UupZkdKY9OF8Q">2.55</ix:nonFraction> million.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;">Interest</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Interest is payable monthly, on the thirteenth day of each calendar month, beginning on May 13, 2026 and on the maturity date, at a rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_gw05YkuTH0WwOqVaqC56mg" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_PurchasersMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_SeniorNotesMember_5IVP0rdyNk2iM2ER-I-CNQ" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentInterestRateStatedPercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_bB-H0PU8WkGV4yUXEGVJ9A">12.5</ix:nonFraction>% per annum. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;">For the current quarter and current six months, the Company incurred interest expense (including interest paid in cash, and the amortization of deferred finance costs and OID) related to the Secured Notes of approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_SeniorNotesMember_-pouhWEtqEWAr-IzMmMnog" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:InterestExpenseDebt" scale="6" id="Narr_TeVMnSCT2EK37iljd4a7sA"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_SeniorNotesMember_j0Jln-9Dv0eCN07t9Ji5Lg" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:InterestExpenseDebt" scale="6" id="Narr_7rpW7BaUlkG-dZOsLXmnFA">0.25</ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction> million. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="margin-bottom:12pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;">Deferred Finance Costs and Other Reductions to Carrying Value of Debt</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;">In connection with the issuance of the Secured Notes in April 2026, the Company incurred various fees and costs totaling $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="As_Of_4_30_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_PurchasersMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_SeniorNotesMember_T9OHrEY5ckKsy8BeJhW2Pg" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DeferredFinanceCostsGross" scale="6" id="Narr_JW_wb9h990GQWs7EE7iT2w">0.35</ix:nonFraction> million, which were deferred on the Company&#8217;s balance sheet as a reduction of the carrying value of the related debt. Also in connection with the issuance of the Secured Notes in April 2026, the Company issued shares of common stock as described above. In accordance with applicable GAAP, the Company allocated the value of the total proceeds between the debt and the shares of common stock, based on the relative fair values of each; as a result, the Company recognized a $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2026_To_4_30_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_FirstEagleAlternativeCreditLlcMember__f4s5NsMlESSLcW34ceyXQ" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ProceedsFromIssuanceOfWarrants" scale="6" id="Narr_xblIHQNwMUmiFOzh2lYSBA">0.12</ix:nonFraction> million increase to stockholders&#8217; equity as additional paid-in capital for the allocated fair value of the shares, and an offsetting decrease to the net carrying value of the debt. These reductions to the carrying value of the Secured Notes (plus the impact of the original issue discount of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2026_To_4_30_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_PurchasersMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_SeniorNotesMember_gf_ZjfTJckiu-exxpHgcUA" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:AmortizationOfDebtDiscountPremium" scale="6" id="Narr_OWpchi5qX0udzl36efATdA">0.41</ix:nonFraction> million) totaling $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2026_To_4_30_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_PurchasersMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_SeniorNotesMember_gf_ZjfTJckiu-exxpHgcUA" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:AmortizationOfFinancingCostsAndDiscounts" scale="6" id="Narr_m3sQLrZ2dEGLb5_ekQoFsA">0.88</ix:nonFraction> million are being amortized to interest expense over the term of the debt using the effective interest method. </p></ix:continuation><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="margin-bottom:12pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">17</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:79.3%;border:0;margin:30pt 10.35% 30pt 10.35%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:10.35%;padding-right:10.35%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;min-height:41.75pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 30pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;">XCEL BRANDS,&#160;INC. AND SUBSIDIARIES</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;">Notes&#160;to Unaudited Condensed Consolidated Financial Statements</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;">June 30, 2026</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">(Unaudited)</p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="margin-bottom:12pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_AOf8Oz5EykGUyJMcCLhuDw" name="us-gaap:StockholdersEquityNoteDisclosureTextBlock" id="Tb_JRcfw01u106WkKc22-Vhyw" continuedAt="Tb_JRcfw01u106WkKc22-Vhyw_cont1" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">7. &#160; &#160;Stockholders&#8217; Equity &#160; </b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;">Equity Line Facility</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">On January 21, 2026, the Company entered into a common stock purchase agreement with White Lion Capital, LLC (&#8220;White Lion&#8221;), pursuant to which White Lion has committed to purchase up to $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="Duration_1_21_2026_To_1_21_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_WhiteLionCapitalLlcMember_gSNcpUpnLEWKJtEAkeXIIg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xelb:CommonStockPurchaseCommitmentAmount" scale="6" id="Narr_iIDzPWT5BUedh1oeGulj_g">15.0</ix:nonFraction> million of the Company&#8217;s common stock. Under the terms and conditions of this agreement, the Company has the right, but not the obligation, to sell to White Lion, and White Lion is obligated to purchase, up to $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="Duration_1_21_2026_To_1_21_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_WhiteLionCapitalLlcMember_gSNcpUpnLEWKJtEAkeXIIg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xelb:CommonStockPurchaseCommitmentAmount" scale="6" id="Narr_yaTiSSrQs0iHAZEQ4Ur7ZQ">15.0</ix:nonFraction> million of the Company&#8217;s common stock. The actual amount and timing of any sales of Common Stock will be determined by the Company at its discretion.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The aggregate number of shares that the Company can sell White Lion under this agreement is limited to and may not exceed <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_aOdaQld8FkuFmrvdGtgC-w" contextRef="Duration_1_21_2026_To_1_21_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_WhiteLionCapitalLlcMember_gSNcpUpnLEWKJtEAkeXIIg" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xelb:MaximumSharesIssuableUnderEquityLine" scale="0" id="Narr_zfOHPlNka0-Y_XiACIYhWQ">1,178,173</ix:nonFraction> shares (subject to adjustment for any reorganization, recapitalization, non-cash dividend, stock split, reverse stock split, or other similar transaction), which is equal to <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_gw05YkuTH0WwOqVaqC56mg" contextRef="Duration_1_21_2026_To_1_21_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_WhiteLionCapitalLlcMember_gSNcpUpnLEWKJtEAkeXIIg" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xelb:PercentageOfEquitySecuritiesIssuedOrIssuable" scale="-2" id="Narr_qAFdwHagTUWUIgGaSpG9pA">19.99</ix:nonFraction>% of the total shares of the Company&#8217;s common stock outstanding immediately prior to the execution of the agreement, unless (i) the Company obtains stockholder approval to issue additional shares in excess of this amount, or (ii) the average price paid for all shares of Common Stock issued under the agreement equals or exceeds certain levels as specified in the agreement.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">In consideration for White Lion&#8217;s execution and entry into such arrangement, the Company agreed to issue White Lion $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="Duration_1_21_2026_To_1_21_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_WhiteLionCapitalLlcMember_gSNcpUpnLEWKJtEAkeXIIg" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xelb:CommonStockIssuedAsCommitmentFee" scale="0" id="Narr_NGJ0rBPktUCdUdbfFisMjw">37,500</ix:nonFraction>&#160;worth of common stock, with the number of shares issued determined based on the closing price of the Company&#8217;s stock on the business day immediately preceding the day on which the related registration statement is declared effective by the SEC; accordingly, the Company issued <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_aOdaQld8FkuFmrvdGtgC-w" contextRef="Duration_1_21_2026_To_1_21_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_WhiteLionCapitalLlcMember_gSNcpUpnLEWKJtEAkeXIIg" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xelb:StockIssuedDuringPeriodSharesConsiderationForEntryIntoEquityLineFacility" scale="0" id="Narr_Ot8JoZGvG0OzDQy1EDm1Ng">16,094</ix:nonFraction> shares to White Lion on May 6, 2026. Additionally, pursuant to the terms of an advisory agreement between the Company and Maxim Group LLC, the Company agreed to pay Maxim Group LLC a cash fee equal to&#160;<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_gw05YkuTH0WwOqVaqC56mg" contextRef="Duration_1_21_2026_To_1_21_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_WhiteLionCapitalLlcMember_gSNcpUpnLEWKJtEAkeXIIg" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xelb:EquityIssuanceFeePercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_19hme2MUpESBg7OyuRsqNw">4.0</ix:nonFraction>% of the gross proceeds received from any sales of securities to White Lion under this arrangement. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">For the three and six months ended June 30, 2026, the Company issued an aggregate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_aOdaQld8FkuFmrvdGtgC-w" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_WhiteLionCapitalLlcMember_YacU1nRwPk6eauC339Z8Zw" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:StockIssuedDuringPeriodSharesNewIssues" scale="0" id="Narr_2rudvIz3KkWLpM8N5mNovw"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_aOdaQld8FkuFmrvdGtgC-w" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_WhiteLionCapitalLlcMember_PKlSHYpRi0CNbc-8lMwelw" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:StockIssuedDuringPeriodSharesNewIssues" scale="0" id="Narr_ETTj-lCkKkeTOtPCbx2fGQ">348,000</ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction> shares under the equity line facility arrangement and received aggregate net proceeds of approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_WhiteLionCapitalLlcMember_YacU1nRwPk6eauC339Z8Zw" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ProceedsFromIssuanceOfCommonStock" scale="6" id="Narr_bte7sBgJ30uhjhK1T6ZCXw"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_WhiteLionCapitalLlcMember_PKlSHYpRi0CNbc-8lMwelw" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ProceedsFromIssuanceOfCommonStock" scale="6" id="Narr_kuog0RL_RUyTt4iy-Ij5Ug">0.67</ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction> million. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Also, during the current six months, the Company incurred approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_SeNoRWdIwkmrWeisC2LdDQ" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xelb_WhiteLionCapitalLlcMember_YacU1nRwPk6eauC339Z8Zw" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:AdjustmentsToAdditionalPaidInCapitalStockIssuedIssuanceCosts" scale="6" id="Narr_UNfQIbYy_0a6gQ3fs3i66Q">0.26</ix:nonFraction> million of fees and expenses (consisting of legal and accounting fees) associated with the equity line arrangement and related registration statement, which were recorded as a reduction to additional paid-in capital. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Equity Incentive Plans</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">A total of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_aOdaQld8FkuFmrvdGtgC-w" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_PlanNameAxis_xelb_EquityIncentivePlan2021Member_0Yomt-p67kubYBAs29M78Q" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ShareBasedCompensationArrangementByShareBasedPaymentAwardNumberOfSharesAuthorized" scale="0" id="Narr_5-ndw3bvfU6bRsnSZm2fyQ">1,150,000</ix:nonFraction> shares of common stock are eligible for issuance under the Company&#8217;s 2021 Equity Incentive Plan (the &#8220;2021 Plan&#8221;). The 2021 Plan provides for the grant of any or all of the following types of awards: stock options (incentive or non-qualified), restricted stock, restricted stock units, performance awards, or cash awards. The 2021 Plan is administered by the Company&#8217;s Board of Directors, or, at the Board&#8217;s discretion, a committee of the Board. In addition, <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_aOdaQld8FkuFmrvdGtgC-w" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_PlanNameAxis_xelb_EquityIncentivePlan2011Member_E2QUPkCVWUmWumN-h0EGRA" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ShareBasedCompensationArrangementByShareBasedPaymentAwardOptionsOutstandingNumber" scale="0" id="Narr_fd9VVjPcbESrJdItOFn3RA">10,000</ix:nonFraction> stock options previously granted under the Company&#8217;s 2011 Equity Incentive Plan (the &#8220;2011 Plan&#8221;) remain outstanding and shares of common stock may be issued to satisfy options previously granted under the 2011 Plan, although <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_aOdaQld8FkuFmrvdGtgC-w" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_PlanNameAxis_xelb_EquityIncentivePlan2011Member_E2QUPkCVWUmWumN-h0EGRA" decimals="INF" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:ShareBasedCompensationArrangementByShareBasedPaymentAwardNumberOfSharesAvailableForGrant" scale="0" id="Narr_fKnqqgG3akSfTkoOJFdxuA">no</ix:nonFraction> new awards may be granted under the 2011 Plan.</p><p st